  clock: 4  # 2bb9
  nonce: 2bb9  # 2bb9
  message: "how big of a deal is the \"wrapper functions (commands.takeScreenshot()) that don't contain literal command names\" gap? and might there be analogous issues in frameworks other than Tauri or languages other than Rust?"  # 2bb9
- op: discuss  # 8892
  at: '2026-03-11T18:15:50Z'  # 8892
  by: agent  # 8892
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 8892
  clock: 5  # 8892
  nonce: '8892'  # 8892
  message: "Impact: Moderate. 38% of commands (122/323) across 4 Tauri repos were unreachable through literal invoke matching. Now fixed in PR #2165 (specta wrapper resolution). Analogous issues exist in Electron IPC (contextBridge wrappers), GraphQL codegen (useGetUsersQuery hooks), gRPC generated clients, and wasm_bindgen facade modules."  # 8892
- op: discuss  # a408
  at: '2026-03-15T21:02:44Z'  # a408
  by: human  # a408
  actor: jgstern  # a408
  clock: 6  # a408
  nonce: a408  # a408
  message: "if there are analogous issues, doesn't that imply we've discovered an invariant? are there any existing invariants that would capture these kinds of issues?"  # a408
- op: discuss  # 30d9
  at: '2026-03-16T04:06:05Z'  # 30d9
  by: agent  # 30d9
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 30d9
  clock: 7  # 30d9
  nonce: 30d9  # 30d9
  message: "Good point. The invariant would be: 'Generated wrapper/proxy functions must not break cross-language edge tracing. When a linker detects a bridge call (IPC, RPC, WASM, codegen), it must trace through wrapper layers to connect the application-level call site to the implementation.'\n\nNo existing invariant captures this — the route-to-handler invariant (INV-nimik) covers route→handler resolution but not IPC/RPC wrapper tracing. This is a distinct pattern: codegen-mediated indirection.\n\nAffected frameworks: Tauri specta (fixed), Electron contextBridge (partially fixed), GraphQL codegen hooks (not addressed), gRPC generated clients (partially — proto→Go works but not codegen wrappers in TS/Python), wasm_bindgen facade modules (not addressed).\n\nShould I create an invariant for this? Something like 'INV: Codegen wrapper tracing — cross-language linkers must resolve through generated binding/proxy layers'?"  # 30d9
- op: discuss  # 1610
  at: '2026-03-16T04:24:59Z'  # 1610
  by: human  # 1610
  actor: jgstern  # 1610
  clock: 8  # 1610
  nonce: '1610'  # 1610
  message: "yes please do create such an invariant. it should be in a \"violated\" state since we haven't actually checked on those other situations. it can be low priority but it still should be presumed violated."  # 1610
